  "compiler_architecture": {
    "lexer_notes": "The lexer must support Unicode for IAST transliteration, handle sandhi-based token merging, and treat special characters like Visarga (h) and Anusvara (m) as distinct semantic modifiers.",
    "parser_notes": "The parser should be SOV-oriented (Subject-Object-Verb). Karaka mapping dictates AST node relationship: Karta -> Kriya node, Karma -> Kriya input. Samasa-based compounds form nested identifier structures.",
    "type_system_notes": "Sanskrit's gender/number/case system maps to type inference: Vibhakti indicates Type Category (e.g., Nominative = Type/Class), while Samasa acts as structural typing or composition.",
    "recommended_rust_structures": "Enum `Vibhakti` (Prathama, Dvitīyā...), Struct `Dhatu` (Root, Gana), Enum `SamasaType` (Tatpurusha...), Struct `ASTNode` (Subject, Object, Verb, Modifier)."
  }
